nt for Democrats keeps this short of Safe R.", "watch": "A late wave of Democratic outside spending or an even stronger national environment could narrow the margin, as could traction from reports on Strada's home-inspection business.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 89 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Daniel Webster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Republicans are favored to hold Florida's 11th District, where Daniel Webster's retirement opened a seat that leans Republican by about seven points. Joe Strada, a businessman who won a narrow primary decided by a recount, enters the general with a large financial edge, having raised roughly $5.5 million to James Pericola's $226,000, along with outside support. Ten race raters place the district in the Republican column, six calling it Solid or Safe Republican.\n\nThe Democratic side's best evidence is the political environment and a July poll showing the candidates tied, though that survey was sponsored by a Democratic firm and is now months old. Prediction markets give Pericola roughly a one-in-seven chance of winning. A Libertarian candidate also appears on the ballot. The race would likely move only with a major late shift in spending or national conditions.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -7.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1312, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1199, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1239, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1092, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0593, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-